Confident, I was.  Since posting about my great progress earlier this
week, I used and abused my resources such that I thought I might have
a chance to ascend without even wishing.  I did have a nervous scrape
with a master mind flayer, but he killed himself with his own wand of
death and my shield of reflection.  I later genocided them on a
throne.

After mopping up the castle with my -39AC, yawning through the four
castle dragons, I looted the wand, brought it back up to my stash, and
considered trying a wishless game, but ended up using it for magic
markers, charging, genocide, and speed boots.  I reverse genocided
tengus twice and finally got my intrinsic, burned through my magic
markers topping off the enchantment on my gear, genocided all mimics
in anticipation of the shops in orcus town, consolidated my inventory,
made holy water, and headed down into Gehennom.

The melee in the first few maze levels served to perpetuate my
confidence; I felt invincible.  Asmodeus was annoying until I dragged
him down with me into the swamp and stand on the up stairs.  He died
pretty quickly, and I had a look around before getting engulfed by
Juiblex.  I could probably have killed him from inside, I thought, but
to be safe, I zapped a wand of digging and smacked him.  OK, now let's
see about testing this amulet I found on a demon on the last level...

